# Line endings that are load-bearing inside container images.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf = true, which rewrites LF to CRLF on
# checkout. For a shell script that is COPYied into a Linux image that is fatal, and the
# error is unhelpfully indirect: `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` makes the kernel look for an
# interpreter literally named "bash\r" and the container dies with
# "bad interpreter: No such file or directory". Pin these to LF regardless of platform.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile text eol=lf

# Shipped as-is; never newline-translated.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
